@@ -197,6 +205,8 @@ _Generated by /synthesise. One file written; all source files untouched. Re-run
 
 Drop sections that have nothing to say (e.g. no contradictions found) rather than padding them. Keep it the minimum viable state file — signal density over completeness.
 
+**The YAML frontmatter is the machine anchor — always write it.** It's how the rest of the loop reads this file: `/os-start` reads `last-updated` for the staleness flag in its briefing; `/os-save` re-stamps it on every save (`updated-by: os-save (synthesise)`, and `last-full-synthesise` when it does a full re-anchor). A re-run **overwrites** `current-state.md` by default — that's the compounding behaviour, and git keeps the history. The only exception: if an existing `current-state.md` is in a clearly different/foreign format (not this schema and not os-save-stamped), ask once before overwriting it (interactive runs only; headless overwrites and says so). Set `updated-by: synthesise` on a file `/synthesise` authored; consumers update these fields in place rather than rewriting them. `last-full-synthesise` = today on a first/full run, carried forward on an incremental one.
